Date: Sun, 21 Jun 2026 19:10:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03330/11362] [outer-loop] arc: TTT solve test -- 0/4, the real
 bottleneck is GOAL-INDUCTION not dynamics

Solve test through the cell-recall-gated engine on the 4 firing games: FULL(L0+CNN) 0/4 and
CNN-ONLY(generalization) 0/4. Root cause is NOT dynamics quality or the exact-execution divergence
-- it is n_win_states=0 for all games: plan_in_model returns 'no plan to is_level_complete' because
the goal detector is EMPTY. Confirmed the cause: the captured corpus has level_before=level_after=0
for EVERY transition in EVERY game (data/arc_transition_corpus/*.npz lb/la all zeros) -- the
capture/ingestion never recorded level progression, so there is no win-state to plan toward.

Decisive gate conclusion: the prior+TTT improves DYNAMICS PREDICTION (the wrong bottleneck);
solving unseen games is GOAL-INDUCTION-bound. Even the cell-recall gate fix (4/5 fires) cannot
produce a solve without a goal. The 0.08 hidden-game wall is goal-induction-bound for the TTT path.
NOT gate-ready; do not spend a scarce L4x4 shot on the prior+TTT.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
